/* Le027 â€” 8-bit characters and case-insensitive keyword tolerance in lexer
   Defect: a lexer that rewrites every byte >= 0x80 to space rejects
   embedded Latin-1 in comments. This file emits:
     - a Part-21 comment containing raw Latin-1 degree-sign 0xB0 ("degC")
     - the magic line in lowercase ("iso-10303-21;") to exercise
       case-insensitive keyword recognition
     - mixed-case ENDSEC and END-ISO-10303-21 to round-trip the test
   A correct lexer should canonicalise keyword case and pass through 8-bit
   bytes inside comments and strings without rewriting. */
iso-10303-21;
HEADER;
FILE_DESCRIPTION(('Le027 - 8-bit chars and case-insensitive keywords'),'2;1');
